===persian===

عمداً... به اتفاق...
از زیرِ ابر گذر کردیم...
بارانِ اتفاق از ابرِ عمد بارید...
دلی که خاکی‌تر بود... خیس‌تر شد...
۱۳۷۳/۴/۵

===machine===

On purpose... by chance...
we passed under a cloud...
The rain of chance fell out of the cloud of purpose...
The heart that was dustier... got the wetter...
1373/4/5

===lantern===

On purpose... by chance...
we passed beneath a cloud.
The rain of chance fell from the cloud of purpose.
The heart that was the dustier got the wetter.

1373/4/5

===translation===

===footnotes===

عمد and اتفاق — on purpose and by accident — are set side by side in the first line and
swapped in the third, so that the deliberate cloud rains an accidental rain. The last line settles
it: whichever it was, the outcome went to whoever needed it most.
